      "voiceover_script": "Two streams appear. Primary market research is the collection and collation of original data via direct contact with potential or existing consumers, also called field research. Questionnaires, interviews, focus groups and observation feed it. Secondary market research uses information that has already been collected and is available for use by others, also called desk research. Competitor websites, government sources, market reports and trade magazines feed that one. One stream is fresh and specific; the other is quick and cheap.",
