      "voiceover_script": "A questionnaire is a set of questions to be answered as a means of collecting data for primary market research. Ticks fill a grid as answers land. Interviews and focus groups go deeper: a group of people representative of the target market discusses opinions about products and promotions. Watch the wording trap. A leading question, Don't you love our menu, pushes people to agree. A neutral question, How often would you order lunch, gives cleaner data. Bad wording distorts every chart that follows.",
