      "voiceover_script": "A sample is a group of people selected to respond to a primary market research exercise, such as a questionnaire. Here is a grid of one hundred city workers. First, random sampling: every cell has an equal chance, and twenty cells light up in scattered positions. Next, quota sampling: the grid sorts into age bands, and the researcher picks ten from each band, so the mix matches the target market. Random selection spreads chance; quota selection controls the mix. Both beat asking only friends.",
