      "voiceover_script": "Sample bias is the pitfall. Lumen Eats surveys thirty people outside one gym, and the grid glows in one corner only. Because that sample came from one place, therefore it over represented fitness fans, so the lunch estimate looked far too high. Accuracy depends on sample size, sample bias, question wording, timing and the age of the data. A larger, more representative sample improves reliability. A biased one makes results misleading, however polished the chart looks.",
