      "voiceover_script": "The stages are clear: set the objective, choose the method, draw the sample, collect, analyse, then recommend. On the split screen, primary data is specific and current, yet costly and prone to bias. Secondary data is quick and cheap, yet generic and possibly outdated. Because this decision is about a local launch, therefore Lumen Eats pays for a neutral survey, so the recommendation rests on fresh evidence. The best research often blends both streams, with a checked sample and careful wording.",
